coder › Done. All changes are on branch `add-env-config`, committed in small pieces.

What changed
- `src/env.ts` (new): `fromEnv(env, prefix = 'APP_')` reads `${prefix}PORT`, `${prefix}HOST`, `${prefix}DEBUG`, `${prefix}NAME`. Port becomes a number, debug becomes a boolean (`true/1/yes` → true, `false/0/no` → false, case-insensitive), host/name stay strings. Absent or `''` values are left out. A non-numeric port throws `TypeError` naming the variable; an unrecognized debug value throws `TypeError` naming the variable.
- `src/config.ts`: added `validate(config)` — returns the config, or throws a `TypeError` naming the field for a non-integer/out-of-range port (1–65535) or empty host/name.
- `src/index.ts`: `resolveConfig(file, env)` now layers defaults → file → environment and validates; `env` defaults to `process.env`.
- Tests: new `src/env.test.ts` and `src/config.test.ts`, and `src/index.test.ts` extended for layering/validation and the `process.env` default.

